<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><fdroid><repo icon="icon.png" name="Nothing Modes" pubkey="" timestamp="1789028916" url="https://nothing-modes.vercel.app/fdroid/repo" version="20002"><description>Self-hosted F-Droid repository for Nothing Modes</description></repo><application id="com.tdvorak.nothingmodes"><id>com.tdvorak.nothingmodes</id><added>2026-09-10</added><lastupdated>2026-09-10</lastupdated><name>Nothing Modes</name><summary>Automation for Nothing phones</summary><desc>Nothing Modes is an open-source Android automation app for Nothing phones.

Modes persist and restore, and fire on real events. Glyph lights respond.
No cloud, no telemetry.

- Modes: Sleep, Work, Gaming. A mode holds a set of toggles and reverts them when it ends.
- Modes can also fire on triggers for time, battery, screen, notifications, connectivity, geofences, and more.
- Conditions: gate execution with AND logic.
- Actions: 37+ types, including Glyph patterns and Shizuku-backed system toggles.

This self-hosted repository keeps every feature. Users of the official F-Droid
build would lose Nothing's proprietary Glyph SDK and Google Play Services.
